{"id":"2689417f-1e1a-4131-9faf-ad1e610b6e19","revision":0,"last_node_id":26,"last_link_id":38,"nodes":[{"id":1,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[0,-380],"size":[2280,300],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Arbor · XY plot: seed × prompt (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo)\n\nThe classic XY plot, without a single extra node per value.\n\n1. Type the **x** values in *x · seeds* (one per line) and the **y** prompts in *y · prompts*.\n2. **XY Lists** (*cross*) turns them into every combination as plain data — x feeds the sampler's seed, y the prompt — so the sampler simply runs once per pair (3 × 3 = 9 pictures). The *combinations* Panel shows the pairs.\n3. **Image Grid** with XY Lists' *shape* lays the pictures out and labels them by itself — rows are the seeds, columns the prompts. The **Compare Viewer** flips through them.\n\nAny widget can be the x or the y: connect XY Lists' outputs to a sampler's steps, a LoRA strength, a resolution — whatever you want to compare."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Arbor · XY plot: seed × prompt (Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo)\n\nThe classic XY plot, without a single extra node per value.\n\n1. Type the **x** values in *x · seeds* (one per line) and the **y** prompts in *y · prompts*.\n2. **XY Lists** (*cross*) turns them into every combination as plain data — x feeds the sampler's seed, y the prompt — so the sampler simply runs once per pair (3 × 3 = 9 pictures). The *combinations* Panel shows the pairs.\n3. **Image Grid** with XY Lists' *shape* lays the pictures out and labels them by itself — rows are the seeds, columns the prompts. The **Compare Viewer** flips through them.\n\nAny widget can be the x or the y: connect XY Lists' outputs to a sampler's steps, a LoRA strength, a resolution — whatever you want to compare."},"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":3,"type":"Arbor_Panel","pos":[0,0],"size":[300,200],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"数据","name":"data","shape":